		{"id":"e7c57e9a323f65f4","type":"text","text":"# Storage via Retrieval Gateway","x":-284,"y":-640,"width":520,"height":50},
		{"id":"615c2ba9afcd4ff4","type":"text","text":"### External\n- Remove Environmental Distractions\n- Clean up clutter and workspace.","x":-1044,"y":-301,"width":250,"height":193},
		{"id":"d1e8a90ebc8cb5e7","type":"text","text":"### Metacognition\n- Keep in mind the aspects of G.R.I.N.D.E.\n- Ask questions of \"why\" and \"how\"\n- Metacognition is the key to higher order thinking.","x":-1043,"y":447,"width":249,"height":291},
		{"id":"31fc222009147cda","type":"text","text":"# Encoding","x":-625,"y":-392,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"56e2b473e89e2a67","type":"text","text":"### Internal\n- Pray\n- 5 Deep Breaths\n- Clear the mind","x":-1044,"y":-75,"width":250,"height":150},
		{"id":"0e35f040fe6bb7da","type":"text","text":"### G.R.I.N.D.E (Justin Sung)\n\n- Think about\n\t- Grouping\n\t- Relationships\n\t- Interconnected\n\t- Non-Verbal\n\t- Directional\n\t- Emphasized\n- Do this while **encoding**.\n\nIncreases cognitive load, promote proper encoding, creates more direction for a better mind map.\n\n","x":416,"y":-301,"width":250,"height":465},
		{"id":"176c6ad01613ecb3","type":"text","text":"### General Metacognition\n\n- Ask questions\n- Formulate synthesis.\n- Make predictions.\n- Do this while **conducting preliminary** and **encoding**.","x":416,"y":210,"width":250,"height":288},
		{"id":"a925b4eefe9b40a9","type":"text","text":"### Time Management\n- Work in blocks of 45 minutes.\n- Take 10 minute breaks.\n- Avoid doom scrolling or anything **dopamine heavy** during breaks.","x":796,"y":-274,"width":247,"height":319},
		{"id":"4367d6f80e172371","type":"text","text":"### Recommendations (Justin Sung)\n\n- Mind mapping is a skill.\n- Skill takes progress.\n- Focus on building each step of the process **one at a time**.","x":795,"y":195,"width":247,"height":319},
		{"id":"748aea719c8a7882","type":"text","text":"### Preliminary\n- Skim over proceeding topics.\n- Ask questions, create hypothesis, and make predictions.\n- Get a \"lay of the land.\"","x":-1044,"y":118,"width":250,"height":267},
		{"id":"ed64547144fe468f","type":"text","text":"# Retrieval","x":-147,"y":-392,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"de94e6c5896f1f9f","type":"text","text":"### Within a Topic\n\n- Continue reading onto another sub-topic.\n- Repeat encoding process.","x":-147,"y":-130,"width":250,"height":248},
		{"id":"cdc6b56c53c7d28b","type":"text","text":"### After a Topic\n- Grab a new sheet of paper.\n- Rebuild mind map from memory\n- Find errors and revise.\n- Organize content and relationships in a BETTER SCHEMA.","x":-147,"y":151,"width":250,"height":334},
		{"id":"50bca586500f8bc7","type":"text","text":"### 1. Consuming\n- Read a sub-topic for about 10-20 minutes.","x":-626,"y":-130,"width":250,"height":157},
		{"id":"8d82d31e3a7da155","type":"text","text":"### 2. Recollection\n- Spend 60 seconds just thinking and absorbing the fresh information.","x":-626,"y":68,"width":250,"height":157},
		{"id":"d59320fd362a1f28","type":"text","text":"### 3. Mind Map\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\n- Recall the information into a current or new mind map.\n- Mimic how YOUR brain remembers the information.\n- Build relationships and groups.\n- Refer back to material if needed","x":-625,"y":262,"width":249,"height":418}
